[0.010, "o", "14: style, missed edge cases, security smells — before anything is considered done.\r\n15: \r\n16: ## Demo\r\n17: \r\n18: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b610da-8ec0-40ae-a503-2abd38c42020\r\n19: \r\n20: The full pipeline running end-to-end against a 7-issue benchmark: issue in,\r\n21: plan produced, code written, tested inside an isolated Docker sandbox,\r\n22: reviewed, and a final success-rate summary printed out.\r\n23: \r\n24: ## Demo\r\n25: \r\n26: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b610da-8ec0-40ae-a503-2abd38c42020\r\n27: \r\n28: The full pipeline running end-to-end against a 7-issue benchmark: issue in,\r\n29: plan produced, code written, tested inside an isolated Docker sandbox,\r\n30: reviewed, and a final success-rate summary printed out.\r\n31: \r\n32: ## Architecture\r\n33: \r\n34: 1. **Planner agent** — takes an issue description, produces a structured plan\r\n35:    (root cause hypothesis, files to touch, ordered subtasks)\r\n36: 2. **Coder agent** — reads relevant files and writes a patch, using tool calls\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n37:    (read_file, write_file, run_tests)\r\n38: 3. **Test runner** — runs the target repo's own test suite inside an isolated\r\n39:    Docker sandbox; failures are fed back to the coder agent for another attempt\r\n40: 4. **Reviewer agent** — critiques the passing diff against a rubric before\r\n41:    it's considered mergeable\r\n42: 5. **Memory store** — a vector database of past fixes and human feedback,\r\n43:    retrieved and injected into future prompts so the agent improves over time\r\n44: \r\n45: ## Status\r\n"]
