[0.010, "o", "10: hopes for the best. This project is different: it's built around a **feedback\r\n11: loop**. If a fix breaks a test, the agent sees the failure and tries again\r\n12: (up to a capped number of retries) instead of giving up or silently failing.\r\n13: A separate reviewer agent then checks the diff for things tests don't catch —\r\n14: style, missed edge cases, security smells — before anything is considered done.\r\n15: \r\n16: \r\n17: ## Architecture\r\n18: \r\n19: 1. **Planner agent** — takes an issue description, produces a structured plan\r\n20:    (root cause hypothesis, files to touch, ordered subtasks)\r\n"]
